      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A rare type of coronary arteriovenous fistula with multiple supplying vessels from both coronary arteries and draining into the pulmonary artery was found in a 52-year-old woman with angina pectoris. The fistula was successfully closed by division of the vessels draining into the pulmonary artery."},
